@@ -10,3 +10,8 @@ Prices are integer cents everywhere.
 An order can take one discount code with `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`: `SPRING10` (10 % off the items) or
 `WELCOME5` (5.00 € off items of 30.00 € or more). Totals show `discountCents`; shipping is never discounted and
 free shipping is decided on the items before the discount. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+`exportMonth(month)` (`YYYY-MM`) returns the month's orders as CSV text for a spreadsheet: a header line, then one
+line per order by number, with columns `order,date,customer,total` (the total in euros with two decimals, what the
+customer pays). Customers' email and phone are deliberately left out. Fields with a comma or a quote are quoted; a
+month without orders gives the header alone; a malformed month throws a `RangeError`.
