+
+## Request
+
+The accountant wants a monthly export of the orders for her spreadsheet. Add `exportMonth(month)` to the order
+book: `month` is `YYYY-MM`; it returns CSV text with a header line and one line per order placed in that month,
+by order number.
+
+- Columns, in order: `order` (number), `date` (as stored), `customer` (name), `total` (what the
+  customer pays — items - discount + shipping — in euros with two decimals, e.g. `12.50`).
+- A value containing a comma or a quote is quoted as usual in CSV (quotes doubled).
+- A month with no orders gives the header line alone.
+- A month that is not `YYYY-MM` throws a `RangeError`.
+- Lines are separated by `\n`, with no trailing newline.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+Tests in `test/shop.test.ts` cover each rule; `npm test` passes. CHANGELOG and README updated.
+
+## Rework
+
+Rejected by Dana Okafor: the export must not carry customers' email addresses or phone numbers. Columns are now
+`order,date,customer,total` only.
